{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114351","id":3131570403,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc66p_jj","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114351","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114351.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114351.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114351","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114351/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114351/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114351/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5e2bbbc5ed7da47236de006cc2a1ff990c84f19d","number":114351,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prevent update_shape from being called twice on first frame, thus speeding up CSG nodes load times.","user":{"login":"emanvidmaker","id":16447282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDQ3Mjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16447282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker","html_url":"https://github.com/emanvidmaker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emanvidmaker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"due to logic oversight, update_shape can get queued twice to run on the first frame, making scenes csg shapes laggy to open/load in, with this redundant call.\r\n\r\nThis change makes sure that it cant queue twice by marking it as dirty as soon as possible, so it cant queue again.\r\n\r\n---\r\nFound out about the double queue behavior when i was making a benching tool for csg and logging functions calls.\r\nWhere i saw that  \"update_shape\" gets called twice on scene load.\r\n```txt \r\n...\r\nNOTIFICATION_READY --- 0 Microseconds\r\nNOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED --- 7 Microseconds\r\nCSGShape3D::_update_collision_faces --- 68733 Microseconds\r\nCSGShape3D::update_shape --- 1672920 Microseconds\r\nCSGShape3D::_update_collision_faces --- 67424 Microseconds\r\nCSGShape3D::update_shape --- 127781 Microseconds\r\n===-===FRAME 1 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 2 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 3 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 4 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 5 ===-===\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\n A bit of code-base reading later, found out that \"_make_dirty\" 's logic can double queue it on specific but common scenario.  Where its a root shape and not dirty it will call_deferred twice.\r\n\r\nOld code:  (macros removed for clarity)\r\n```cpp \r\nvoid CSGShape3D::_make_dirty(bool p_parent_removing) {\r\n    if ((p_parent_removing || is_root_shape()) && !dirty) {\r\n        callable_mp(this, &CSGShape3D::update_shape).call_deferred(); // ...\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    if (!is_root_shape()) {\r\n        parent_shape->_make_dirty();\r\n    }\r\n    else if (!dirty) {\r\n        callable_mp(this, &CSGShape3D::update_shape).call_deferred();\r\n    }\r\n    dirty = true;\r\n  \r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nby setting `dirty = true;` earlier in the logic it prevents this double queue from happening and calls it once. (since the second queue up looks if dirty is false)\r\n\r\nnew code: (macros removed for clarity)\r\n```cpp \r\nvoid CSGShape3D::_make_dirty(bool p_parent_removing) {\r\n    if ((p_parent_removing || is_root_shape()) && !dirty) {\r\n        callable_mp(this, &CSGShape3D::update_shape).call_deferred(); // ...\r\n        dirty = true; // +++ new code, now the else if will fail if this ran and avoid a requeue\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    if (!is_root_shape()) {\r\n        parent_shape->_make_dirty();\r\n    }\r\n    else if (!dirty) {\r\n        callable_mp(this, &CSGShape3D::update_shape).call_deferred();\r\n    }\r\n    dirty = true;\r\n }\r\n ```\r\n With this fix, it now logs like this:\r\n ```txt\r\n ...\r\n NOTIFICATION_READY --- 0 Microseconds\r\nNOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED --- 6 Microseconds\r\nCSGShape3D::_update_collision_faces --- 67143 Microseconds\r\nCSGShape3D::update_shape --- 1569224 Microseconds\r\n===-===FRAME 1 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 2 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 3 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 4 ===-===\r\n===-===FRAME 5 ===-===\r\n...\r\n```\r\nAnd noticeably reduces scene loading time a second or so, since update_shape can get laggy and now only calls once. \r\n \r\n \r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co